count":2},{"gloss":"conflito","count":1},{"gloss":"rebelião","count":1}]},"G4966":{"id":"G4966","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4966","disambiguated_id":"G4966 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H7927G","headword":"Συχέμ","transliteration":"Suchem","lexical_morphology":"N:N--L","gloss_en":"Shechem","definition_en":"Συχέμ indecl. (Heb. שְׁכֶם), \n Shechem; \n __1. the son of Hamor (Gen.33:19): Act.7:16 b, Rec. \n __2. A city of Samaria (AV, Sychem; in LXX also sometimes Σίκιμα, -ων, as in FlJ): Act.7:16 a,b.†\n (AS)","source_line":5118}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Siquém","count":2}]},"G5251":{"id":"G5251","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5251","disambiguated_id":"G5251 =","unique_id":"G5251","headword":"ὑπερυψόω","transliteration":"huperupsoō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to exalt","definition_en":"ὑπερ-υψόω, -ῶ \n [in LXX: Psa.37:35 (עָרִיץ) Psa.97:9 (עָלָה ni.), Da TH Dan.4:34 11:12 (רוּם), ib. LXX TH Dan.3:52 ff.* ;] \n__1. to exalt beyond measure, exalt to the highest place: Php.2:9. \n __2. to extol (Da, ll. with).†\n (AS)","source_line":5406}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"exaltou-supremamente","count":1}]},"G5347":{"id":"G5347","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5347","disambiguated_id":"G5347 =","unique_id":"G5347","headword":"Φῆστος","transliteration":"Phēstos","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Festus","definition_en":"φῆστος, -ου, ὁ\n (Porcius), Festus, procurator of Judæa: Act.24:27 25:1 ff. Act.26:24-25, 32.†\n (AS)","source_line":5505}],"occurrence_count":13,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Festo","count":13}]},"G565":{"id":"G565","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0565","disambiguated_id":"G0565 =","unique_id":"G0565","headword":"ἀπέρχομαι","transliteration":"aperchomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to go away","definition_en":"ἀπέρχομαι, \n [in LXX chiefly for הלךְ ;] \n __1. to go away, depart (also, in late writers, with \"perfective\" force, to arrive at a destination, the thought being carried on to the goal; M, Pr., 111f., 247; MM, see word); \n__(a) absol.: Mat.13:25, al.; ptcp., ἀπελθών, used pleonastically with other verbs as in Heb. (Dalman, Words, 21), Mat.13:28, al.; \n __(b) with mention of place or person: εἰς, Mat.14:15; ἐπί, Luk.24:24; πρός, Rev.10:9; ἀπό, Luk.1:38; ἐξω, Act.4:15; ἐκεῖ, Mat.2:22. \n __2. As in LXX, before ὀπίσω, with genitive (Heb. הָלַךְ אַחֲרֵי), to go after, follow: Mrk.1:20, Jhn.12:19; metaphorically, Mrk.1:42, Rev.21:1. \n (AS)","source_line":673}],"occurrence_count":117,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"foi","count":37},{"gloss":"foram","count":10},{"gloss":"ir","count":9},{"gloss":"indo","count":7},{"gloss":"saiu","count":5},{"gloss":"foi-embora","count":5},{"gloss":"vá","count":4},{"gloss":"irem","count":4},{"gloss":"fui","count":3},{"gloss":"vai","count":3},{"gloss":"voltaram","count":3},{"gloss":"retiraram","count":2},{"gloss":"ido","count":2},{"gloss":"passou","count":2},{"gloss":"passaram","count":2},{"gloss":"passassem","count":1},{"gloss":"fores","count":1},{"gloss":"entraram","count":1},{"gloss":"chegarem","count":1},{"gloss":"entrareis","count":1},{"gloss":"irão","count":1},{"gloss":"vou","count":1},{"gloss":"vieram","count":1},{"gloss":"saísse","count":1},{"gloss":"voltou","count":1},{"gloss":"tendo-ido-embora","count":1},{"gloss":"vás","count":1},{"gloss":"vades","count":1},{"gloss":"iremos","count":1},{"gloss":"foi-o-chefe","count":1}]},"G628":{"id":"G628","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0628","disambiguated_id":"G0628 =","unique_id":"G0628","headword":"ἀπολούω","transliteration":"apolouō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to wash off","definition_en":"ἀπο-λούω \n [in LXX: Job.9:30 (רָחַץ)* ;] \nto wash off, wash away; mid., metaphorically, with accusative of thing(s), to wash off oneself: ἀμαρτίας, Act.22:16; absol., ἀπελούσασθε, ye washed yourselves clean (cf. Cremer, 406), 1Co.6:11.†\n (AS)","source_line":736}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"lava","count":1},{"gloss":"fostes-lavados","count":1}]},"G650":{"id":"G650","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0650","disambiguated_id":"G0650 =","unique_id":"G0650","headword":"ἀποστερέω","transliteration":"apostereō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to defraud","definition_en":"ἀπο-στερέω, -ῶ\n (στερέω, to rob), [in LXX: Exo.21:10 (גָּרַע), Deu.24:14 (עָשַׁק), Mal.3:5, Sir.4:1 29:6-7 31:21-22 * ;] \nto defraud, deprive of, despoil (in cl. chiefly of the misappropriation of trust funds, Field, Notes, 33; cf. MM, see word): absol., Mrk.10:19, 1Co.6:8; with accusative of person(s), 1Co.7:5. Mid., endure deprivation: 1Co.6:7 (WM, § 38, 3; but see Bl., § 54, 5; M, Pr., 162); pass., ἀπεστερημένοι, bereft of: 1Ti.6:5.†\n (AS)","source_line":759}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"enganador","count":1},{"gloss":"prejuízo","count":1},{"gloss":"prejudicais","count":1},{"gloss":"priveis","count":1},{"gloss":"privadas","count":1}]},"G86":{"id":"G86","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0086","disambiguated_id":"G0086 =","unique_id":"G0086","headword":"ᾍδης","transliteration":"Hadēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"hell: Hades","definition_en":"ᾅδης, -ου, ὁ \n [in LXX ehiefly for שְׁאוֹל, also for דּוּמָה, מָוֶת, etc. ;] \n __1. in Hom., Hades (Pluto), the god of the underworld. \n __2. the abode of Hades, the underivorld; in NT, the abode of departed spirits, Hades: ἐν τ. ᾅ., Luk.16:23; εἰς ᾅ., Act.2:27,31; πύλαι ᾅδου, Mat.16:18; κλεῖς τοῦ ᾅ., Rev.1:18; metaphorically, ἕως ᾅ., Mat.11:23, Luk.10:15; personified, Rev.6:8 20:13,14 (Cremer, 67, 610; MM, VGT, see word).\n † (AS)","source_line":183}],"occurrence_count":10,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"mundo-mortos","count":5},{"gloss":"mortos","count":2},{"gloss":"mundo-dos-mortos","count":2},{"gloss":"o-Hades","count":1}]},"G907":{"id":"G907","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0907","disambiguated_id":"G0907 =","unique_id":"G0907","headword":"βαπτίζω","transliteration":"baptizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to baptize","definition_en":"βαπτίζω \n (βάπτω), [in LXX: 4Ki.5:14 (טבל), Isa.21:4, Jdth.12:7, Sir.31 (34)30 * ;] \nto dip, immerse, sink; \n__1. generally (in Polyb., iii, 72, of soldiers wading breast-deep; in i, 51, of the sinking of ships); metaphorically, to overwhelm (Is, l.with; cf. MM, Exp., x); with cogn. accusative, βάπτισμα β., Mrk.10:38, 39 Luk.12:50. Mid., \n __2. to perform ablutions, wash oneself, bathe (Ki, Jth, Si, ll. with): Mrk.7:4; aor. pass, in same sense, Luk.11:38. \n __3 Of ablution, immersion, as a religious rite, to baptize; \n__(a) (a) absol.; Mrk.1:4, Jhn.1:25, 26 28 3:22, 23, 26 4:2 10:40, 1Co.1:17; ὁ βαπτίζων (= ὁ βαπτιστής, M, Pr., 127), Mrk.6:14, 24; with accusative, Jhn.4:1, Act.8:38, I Co.1.14, 16; with cogn. accusative, τὸ βάπτισμα, Act.19:4 (cf. Mrk.10:38, supr.); pass., to be baptized, receive baptism: Mat.3:13, 14, 16, Mrk.16:16, Luk.3:7, 12 21 7:29 (τ. βάπτισμα) ib. 30, Act.2:41 8:12, 13 36 9:18 10:47 16:15, 33 18:8; mid., 22:16 (M, Pr., 163); \n __(b) with prepositions: ἐν, of the element, Mat.3:6, 11 Mrk.1:4, 5 8, Luk.3:16, Jhn.1:26, 31 33 3:23, Act.1:5 2:38 10:48 11:16, 1Co.10:2; εἰς, of the element, purpose or result (Lft., Notes, 155), Mat.3:1 28:19, Mrk.1:9, Act.8:16 19:3, 5 Rom.6:3, 1Co.1:13, 15 10:2 12:13, Gal.3:27; with dative, ὕδατι, Luk.3:16, Act.1:5 11:16; ὑπὲρ τῶν νεκρῶν, perh. to fulfil the wish of a dead friend, 1Co.15:29 (see ICC, in l.; cf. DB, i, 238ff.; DCG, i, 169a; ii, 605b; Cremer, 126).\n † (AS)","source_line":1025}],"occurrence_count":77,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"batizados","count":19},{"gloss":"batizado","count":17},{"gloss":"batizava","count":5},{"gloss":"batizou","count":4},{"gloss":"batizo","count":3},{"gloss":"batizará","count":3},{"gloss":"batizando","count":3},{"gloss":"batizar","count":3},{"gloss":"fomos-batizados","count":3},{"gloss":"batizei","count